{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy job runs on non-production branch",
    "Explanation": [
      "The pipeline ran green: build, test-production and deploy all succeeded, and the workflow finished with SUCCESS. The behaviour is wrong, though. Pipeline #151 ran on the branch 'koans-08-branch-filters', not 'production', and the deploy job still ran. That breaks the requirement that deploy only runs on commits to production. The cause is that config_6.yml has no branch filtering at all. In CircleCI, 'requires' only controls job ordering and dependencies, so it cannot limit a job to a branch. The fix is to add a branch filter to the deploy job inside the workflow's jobs list, using filters: branches: only: production. CircleCI does not support filters in the top-level job definition. An 'ignore' list of other branches would be fragile, and new branches would still deploy. Build and test-production can keep running on every branch."
    ],
