{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy fails: app files never persisted to workspace",
    "Explanation": [
      "From workflow_3.txt, all three build jobs (build-linux, build-mac, build-windows) succeeded, so builds_green is true. The deploy job failed, so deploy_green is false.",
      "",
      "The job_6.log shows what deploy actually received from the workspace. Only three files were listed: ./meta/linux/build.txt, ./meta/mac/build.txt and ./meta/windows/build.txt. No app files were present, so the first check (test -f app/linux/app.linux) failed with exit code 1. That means workspace_had_apps is false.",
      "",
      "The root cause is in config_8.yml. Each build job generates its app under app/\u003cplatform\u003e/, but its persist_to_workspace step lists only meta/\u003cplatform\u003e under paths. The app directories are never persisted, so attach_workspace (at: .) brings in only the meta files.",
      "",
      "The ruled-out alternatives:",
      "- **change_attach_only:** changing the attach location cannot surface files that were never persisted.",
      "- **remove_verify_only:** dropping the verify step would hide the failure, but the deploy job would still have no apps to store as artifacts.",
      "- **store_artifacts_on_builds_only:** storing artifacts in each build job does not meet the requirement that the deploy job uploads the apps.",
      "- **fix_one_platform_only:** all three platforms have the same omission, so fixing one would still leave deploy failing.",
      "",
      "The correct fix is to add the app paths to each build job's persist_to_workspace. That means adding app/linux, app/windows and app/mac respectively, keeping the meta paths if desired. Deploy will then receive all three apps, pass verification and upload them via store_artifacts."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"builds_green\": true,",
      "  \"deploy_green\": false,",
