{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Missing restore_cache/save_cache keyed on package.json",
    "Explanation": [
      "The log shows the build failed at `yarn install --offline` with \"info No lockfile found.\" and \"Couldn't find any versions for 'left-pad' ... in our cache\". Since the `--offline` flag is fixed and cannot be removed, Yarn must be able to resolve every package from a locally present `~/.cache/yarn` directory. In config_4.yml both the `restore_cache` and `save_cache` steps are commented out, so no cache was ever restored (cache_restored = false) and none was ever saved — hence the empty offline cache that caused the failure. The fix is therefore to uncomment/enable both the `restore_cache` and `save_cache` steps around the install command, with `paths: - ~/.cache/yarn`.",
      "",
      "For the cache key, there is no `yarn.lock` in the repo (\"No lockfile found\"), and the stated requirement is to cache based on `package.json`. So the key must checksum `package.json`, e.g.:",
      "",
      "  key: yarn-packages-v1-{{ checksum \"package.json\" }}",
      "  keys:",
      "    - yarn-packages-v1-{{ checksum \"package.json\" }}",
      "",
      "Caches in CircleCI are immutable — once a key is written it is never overwritten. So to force a new save of the cache when the checksummed file hasn't changed, you bump the version prefix in the key (v1 -\u003e v2), which produces a new, unwritten key and causes a fresh save on the next build."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"cache_restored\": false,",
      "  \"checksum_target\": \"package.json\",",
      "  \"fix\": \"enable_restore_and_save_cache\"",
      "}"
